      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5fca5df4d58780532024a52b|full_name}: 5% is Fine but I'd say 200% is Needed, theres things like Events where someone doesnt want to have to go through individual people and Lower them just to be able to hear the person there talking to, I don't think they where talking about world Volume at all, and yes if they were at an event per say because it was too loud then lowering Voices would also just make it too difficult to hear people they want to talk to half the time. As for people with horrible mics that they cant increase there own Volume to make the quality better due to poor equipment. Or even just people with really soft voices that aren't easily heard, it happens a lot, more then often too, and 150% just doesn't do the job a lot of the time. Theres situations i come across where I have to lower people down to about 40% while having the specific person with a bad mic or soft voice at 150% and still having trouble hearing them.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
